---
import TopNav from '../../components/TopNav.astro';
import SEO from '../../components/SEO.astro';

const faq = [
	{
		q: "What should I do in 6th grade to prepare for college?",
		a: "If you're even remotely interested in math, find out whether your school has an accelerated math program — check the school website, ask a teacher, or ask a parent to help. It's usually decided by 5th and 6th grade test scores and determines whether Algebra I is available to you in 8th grade."
	},
	{
		q: "What do people get wrong about 6th grade and college prep?",
		a: "Not realizing math placement is a decision at all. Getting into Algebra I in 8th grade is what makes Geometry in 9th, Algebra II in 10th, Precalculus in 11th, and Calculus in 12th possible — the track colleges notice. Every district runs placement differently, so it's worth asking exactly how yours decides."
	},
	{
		q: "Does 6th grade count on a college application?",
		a: "No — nothing from 6th grade appears on a college application. But this one math placement decision can shape the next six years of math classes. If math isn't your thing, there's nothing to lose this year by skipping accelerated math."
	},
	{
		q: "What tests or deadlines matter in 6th grade?",
		a: "Whatever placement test your school uses, if it uses one, plus standard state testing in some districts — none of which go on a college application."
	}
];
const faqSchema = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "FAQPage",
	"mainEntity": faq.map((item) => ({
		"@type": "Question",
		"name": item.q,
		"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": item.a }
	}))
};
---

<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="utf-8" />
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
	<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
	<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
	<SEO
		title="6th Grade College Prep: Only One Decision Matters — Six Years Out"
		description="Why your 6th grade math placement is the one decision that shapes the next six years — and how to find out if your school has an accelerated track."
		path="/grades/6"
	/>
	<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
	<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,600;9..144,700&family=Inter:wght@400;500&display=swap">
</head>
<body>
<TopNav current="grades" />

<article class="grade-page">
  <header class="grade-head">
    <div class="grade-badge">6</div>
    <span class="eyebrow">Grade 6</span>
    <h1>Only one decision matters</h1>
    <p class="lede">If math interests you, find out if your school has an accelerated math program.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="grade-section">
    <h2>What to do now</h2>
    <p>If you are even remotely interested in math, put some effort into finding out whether your school has an accelerated math program. If you can get in, this will open up so many doors later on in your education.</p>
    <p>You may be wondering how to find out whether your school even has a gifted and talented or accelerated program for math. My recommendation would be to check your school's website, ask a teacher, or recruit a parent/guardian to figure it out for you.</p>
    <p>If your school doesn't offer anything like this, don't panic — plenty of students still get on track in high school, through a summer course or by doubling up on math for a year.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grade-section">
    <h2>What most people get wrong</h2>
    <p>Not realizing math placement is even a decision at all, specifically a very important one that dictates whether Algebra 1 is even available to you in 8th grade. However, it is typically made based off of 5th and/or 6th grade test scores, so ensure you are prepared for those.</p>
    <p>Getting into Algebra 1 in 8th grade is usually what makes Geometry in 9th, Algebra 2 in 10th, Precalculus in 11th, and Calculus in 12th possible — that's the track colleges notice. Every district runs math placement differently too. Some use a single test, others weigh grades and teacher recommendations, so it's worth asking exactly how yours decides.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grade-section">
    <h2>What counts</h2>
    <p>Nothing from 6th grade makes it to your college application, but that one decision now has the potential to shape the next six years of math.</p>
    <p>And if math isn't your thing, that's completely fine too — there's nothing to lose this year by skipping accelerated math.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grade-section">
    <h2>Tests and deadlines</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>State testing in some places</li>
      <li>Whatever placement test your school uses, if there even is one</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="related">
    <h2>More resources</h2>
    <div class="related-grid">
      <a class="article-card" href="/high-school-classes">
        <h3>How do I choose my high school classes?</h3>
        <p>Picking a freshman-year schedule can feel like guessing — here's how to actually think about it, four years out.</p>
        <span class="read-more">Read more →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="article-card" href="/application">
        <h3>What's actually on a college application?</h3>
        <p>The artifact itself, demystified.</p>
        <span class="read-more">Read more →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="grade-nav">
    <a class="back" href="/timeline">← Back to the timeline</a>
    <a class="next" href="/grades/7">Next grade →</a>
  </nav>
</article>

<style>
:root{
  --paper:#FAF4EA;
  --ink:#12283D;
  --ink-soft:#4A5C70;
  --ink-faint:#7A8899;
  --rule:#E4D9C6;
  --g6:#E6F1FB;
  --g7:#B5D4F4;
  --g8:#85B7EB;
  --g9:#378ADD;
  --g10:#185FA5;
  --g11:#0C447C;
  --g12:#042C53;
}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
body{
  margin:0;
  background:var(--paper);
  color:var(--ink);
  font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;
  font-size:16px;
  line-height:1.6;
  -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
}
.grade-page{max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;padding:80px 24px 120px}
.grade-head{text-align:center;margin-bottom:56px}
.grade-badge{
  width:48px;height:48px;margin:0 auto 20px;border-radius:50%;
  background:var(--g6);border:1px solid var(--g7);color:var(--g12);
  display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
  font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:20px;
}
.eyebrow{display:block;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:var(--g10);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.06em;margin-bottom:14px}
.grade-head h1{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:700;font-size:34px;line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 14px;letter-spacing:-0.01em;text-wrap:balance}
.lede{font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--ink-soft);margin:0}

.grade-section{margin-bottom:40px}
.grade-section h2{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:19px;color:var(--g10);margin:0 0 12px}
.grade-section p{font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--ink);margin:0 0 12px}
.grade-section p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
.grade-section ul{margin:0;padding-left:20px}
.grade-section li{font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--ink);margin-bottom:8px}
.grade-section li:last-child{margin-bottom:0}

.related{margin-bottom:40px}
.related h2{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:19px;color:var(--g10);margin:0 0 16px}
.related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));gap:16px}
.article-card{
  display:block;padding:24px;border-radius:14px;
  background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule);text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);
}
.article-card:hover{border-color:var(--g10)}
.article-card:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--g10);outline-offset:3px}
.article-card h3{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 10px}
.article-card p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--ink-soft);margin:0 0 14px}
.article-card .read-more{font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:var(--g10)}

.grade-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;margin-top:8px}
.back{font-size:14px;color:var(--g10);text-decoration:none;font-weight:500}
.back:hover{text-decoration:underline}
.back:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--g10);outline-offset:3px}
.next{font-size:14px;color:var(--g10);text-decoration:none;font-weight:500}
.next:hover{text-decoration:underline}
.next:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--g10);outline-offset:3px}

@media (max-width:640px){
  .grade-page{padding:56px 20px 96px}
  .grade-head h1{font-size:28px}
}
</style>
</body>
</html>
